1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
 Well, hey everyone, and welcome to The Porch.

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:06,120
 We're going to be diving into the question that's been on everyone's mind.

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:09,320
 Why in the world are women so hard to understand?

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:13,040
 I think what you meant to say was, "Why in the world are men so confusing?"

5
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:17,080
 Okay, so it seems like both genders may have some difficulty understanding each other.

6
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:20,200
 Which is why each week, we're spotlighting a different side of the room

7
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:24,840
 to dig into issues we face within our own gender while growing an understanding for the opposite sex.

8
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:27,560
 One night, we're putting the guys under the microscope.

9
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,160
 The next night is for the girls.

10
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:31,400
 But don't worry, everybody's invited every night.

11
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,920
 Because here's the thing we've figured out.

12
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:35,480
 We're not actually short on opinions about men and women.

13
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,400
 He's saying this.

14
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,400
 She's saying that.

15
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,200
 But what does God have to say about all of it?

16
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,520
 Welcome to the debate that culture can't settle.

17
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,280
 Welcome to what's actually true.

18
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:44,880
 About him.

19
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:45,880
 And about her.

20
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:48,880
 Welcome to your favorite Tuesday night series.

21
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:50,800
 She Said. She Said.

22
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:57,240
 Alright, well Porch, how are we doing tonight?

23
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:58,920
 We doing okay?

24
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:00,840
 It's great to be with you.

25
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:03,560
 Man, I have loved this summer.

26
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,400
 Living through Porch 20.

27
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:11,200
 But man, I am so excited for this series and the next 20 that are still ahead of us.

28
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:14,000
 I am so glad that you are here in this room.

29
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
 If you are new to the space for the very first time, let me be, I hope just one,

30
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,800
 but not the first to welcome you here.

31
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:23,120
 We're so glad that you would give up your Tuesday to be here.

32
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:26,680
 And then to all of our Porch Life family all across the country, we love you guys.

33
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,440
 We're so thankful for what God is doing.

34
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,920
 Not just in here, but out there.

35
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:32,240
 And the fact that you would tune in too.

36
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:34,160
 Some of you, you're watching this right now.

37
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:36,280
 Others of you, you're watching this in the future.

38
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:43,200
 But all together, we are so thankful that you would be a part of what God is doing in the lives of young adults.

39
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:47,920
 Special shout out to three very important Porch Life locations.

40
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,920
 Porch Life Midland.

41
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,960
 Anybody from Midland in the house?

42
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:53,360
 Porch Life Greater Lafayette.

43
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:55,320
 Anybody from Greater Lafayette and Dallas?

44
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,200
 Okay, we got a little bit of love for you guys.

45
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,640
 And then Porch Life Springfield.

46
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:11,960
 Well, hey, just a couple of years ago, my wife and I, we stood on this stage and we announced something very important to our family.

47
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,320
 Well, we're back.

48
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:23,320
 Roll the video.

49
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,280
 That's right, everybody.

50
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:32,440
 Coming in just a few months, we are expecting a little girl.

51
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:34,880
 Yes, yes, yes.

52
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:36,120
 That was my reaction.

53
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,600
 You saw Cash's reaction.

54
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:42,040
 He has no idea what is in store, nor do I.

55
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:48,000
 It only took me walking into Hill House once to realize I have no clue what is actually ahead of me.

56
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,840
 I am completely out of my depth.

57
00:02:50,840 --> 00:03:00,320
 And yet, while we've been processing the news of having a little girl, and I've been wrestling with God about becoming a girl dad.

58
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:04,120
 How crazy is that?

59
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:11,800
 I have been spending a lot of time, yes, reading and researching and listening and trying to catch up with what's happening in the lives of ladies.

60
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:23,280
 But more than that, I've just been talking to God and I've been contemplating everything that I want my daughter to believe is true about her.

61
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:30,600
 Like, I want her to grow up believing that she's valuable, like before she ever accomplishes anything, she is valuable.

62
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:33,360
 I want her to grow up knowing that she's important.

63
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,800
 Like, it doesn't matter how popular she is.

64
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,400
 It doesn't matter how pretty she is.

65
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,400
 It doesn't matter how cool she is.

66
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:43,800
 It doesn't matter what comparison culture tries to serve up to her and tell her how she needs to catch up and match her peers.

67
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:48,080
 I want to know she's important and I want her to know that she's worthy of respect.

68
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:53,080
 Like, that she is by God dignified from birth.

69
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:56,160
 That it doesn't matter what some boy has to say about her.

70
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:58,280
 It doesn't matter what some boss has to say about her.

71
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:01,280
 It does not matter what somebody might say to her in the future.

72
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:09,480
 It is undeniably true that she is valuable, worthy of pursuing.

73
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:18,280
 And as I've thought about her, I've thought about my boy, my son Cash, and I've just been considering the things that I want him to believe are true of himself as well.

74
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:24,480
 Like, I want him to grow up believing his masculinity is not something that he needs to apologize for.

75
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:28,480
 It is something that he can appreciate which God has given him.

76
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:34,480
 I want him to grow up and know that he is exactly who God intended him to be.

77
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:40,480
 Like, under the hood of his heart and all the hardwiring that God has put together, he does not need to feel insecure.

78
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:44,480
 He does not need to be loud and performative to match up with the world.

79
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:50,480
 And he does not need to feel like he needs to make up for some deficiency that the world is telling him he has.

80
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:53,480
 And I want him to know that he has what it takes.

81
00:04:53,480 --> 00:05:00,480
 Like, he can lead when others can't, he can serve when others won't, and he can do what others haven't.

82
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:05,480
 I want my son to know what it means to be a man.

83
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:10,480
 And I want my daughter to know what it means to be a woman.

84
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:14,480
 And I want the same thing for every one of you.

85
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:21,480
 Because as I've been praying about my children, God has not only brought them to mind, he's brought you to mind.

86
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,480
 It's funny.

87
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:27,480
 I don't share that announcement just to get a rise out of the crowd.

88
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,480
 I share it because this is what you do with family.

89
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:32,480
 Like, you celebrate really good news.

90
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:36,480
 And the porch is an extension of mine and Brooke's family.

91
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:38,480
 And so we wanted to bring that to you.

92
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:42,480
 And yet, as we've been praying about our family, I have been thinking about you.

93
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:49,480
 And I want so desperately for you to understand what it is to be a man and what it is to be a woman.

94
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:54,480
 Like, for the guys in the room, I want you to know that your masculinity is not a problem that needs to be fixed.

95
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:57,480
 It is something to be understood and embraced.

96
00:05:57,480 --> 00:06:04,480
 And for the women in the room, I want you to know that your femininity, it is not amounts of meeting beauty standards and finding a man

97
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:10,480
 or becoming a girl boss who doesn't need to find a man, but embracing your God-given dignity and distinctions.

98
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,480
 That's what I want us to know.

99
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:21,480
 I want you to know that despite what modern culture and woke politicians and TikTok influencers or the manosphere or the femmosphere might have to say,

100
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:28,480
 which, if you're paying attention, is about as erratic as confetti in a tornado, your manhood and womanhood matter.

101
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:33,480
 It matters to you. It matters to your family. It matters to our society.

102
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:36,480
 It matters to our city. It matters to our world.

103
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:39,480
 But most of all, it matters to God.

104
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:43,480
 The question is, who gets to decide what a man or a woman is?

105
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:45,480
 Like, for the guys.

106
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:54,480
 Is it Andrew Tate? Is it Dan Bilzerian? Is it David Goggins or Joe Rogan or Mr. Rogers or Uncle Phil?

107
00:06:54,480 --> 00:07:01,480
 For the ladies in the room, like, is it Beyonce? Is it Kylie Jenner? Is it Alex Earl? Is it Alex Cooper?

108
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:05,480
 Is it Martha Stewart? Is it Beth Dutton? Or is it Emily Gilmore?

109
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:12,480
 The fact of the matter is, our society does not have a good definition of what a man or a woman is,

110
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:15,480
 as the aforementioned lists entail.

111
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:20,480
 There are a lot of opinions out there, and a lot of these opinions are not, in fact, good.

112
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:28,480
 Like, for example, some people are saying that men and women are the exact same.

113
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:32,480
 That all you have to do is just swap jerseys if you want to.

114
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:35,480
 That you can pick whatever team you want to play on, whatever you want to play on.

115
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:39,480
 But here's the problem with that, and I want to be gracious in saying this.

116
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:41,480
 The problem with it is reality.

117
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:46,480
 Like, we can just simply read from Genesis 1, verse 27, that God created man,

118
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:48,480
 talking about mankind in his own image.

119
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:53,480
 In the image of God, he created him, male and female.

120
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:55,480
 He created them.

121
00:07:55,480 --> 00:08:00,480
 You see, God wants it to be very clear that we're different from one another.

122
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:06,480
 Men are males, and women are females, which is why gender is not assigned at birth.

123
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:09,480
 Gender is recognized at birth.

124
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:12,480
 Your mind doesn't get to tell you what your body is.

125
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:17,480
 Your body actually is a sign from God what, in fact, your mind should say.

126
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:23,480
 It is recognized by way of your biology in at least four different ways what your specific gender is.

127
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:26,480
 It is recognized through your gender code.

128
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,480
 Men have a Y chromosome.

129
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:30,480
 Women have two X chromosomes.

130
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:32,480
 It is recognized through your genitalia.

131
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:33,480
 Men have penises.

132
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,480
 Women have vaginas.

133
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:37,480
 Yes, in fact, we are going there.

134
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,480
 It is recognized through your hormone chemistry.

135
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:40,480
 Men have testosterone.

136
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:42,480
 Women have estrogen.

137
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,480
 It is recognized through your brain development.

138
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:50,480
 So even if Facebook wants to give you years ago, I think it was '72, I think they have reduced it to '50,

139
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:56,480
 but now there's a custom fill-in feature for you to identify your gender however it is you want to identify.

140
00:08:56,480 --> 00:09:00,480
 And God is very clear that gender is binary.

141
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,480
 It's male and it's female.

142
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:07,480
 Now, let me just be really clear on something.

143
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:11,480
 I can say all of this so simply.

144
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:17,480
 And so many of you, you're ready to receive it quickly because it matches up with your understanding of the world.

145
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:26,480
 And yet there are people in this room, when a space is this large and a crowd is this big, that this is anything but simple to understand.

146
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:28,480
 And so I just -- I want to speak to you.

147
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:38,480
 If that's your story, your experience in the room, if you find yourself wrestling with gender confusion, if you feel trapped in your body,

148
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:48,480
 I just want you to know you're so welcome here, and you do not have to believe to belong in this space.

149
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:50,480
 We would love to get to know you.

150
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,480
 We would love to hear your story.

151
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:53,480
 It would be our joy to journey with you.

152
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:57,480
 And all you have to do is just come up and say hello.

153
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:05,480
 But I also want you to know, if that's you, that your dysphoria, it doesn't get to tell you who you are.

154
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:08,480
 God wants to tell you who you are.

155
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:12,480
 And the beauty of it is, is that God, he's not asking you to come up and meet him where he's at.

156
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:17,480
 He actually has come down to the person of Jesus to meet you where you are.

157
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:25,480
 In his heart, it beats with compassion towards the helpless and the harassed, which we all were once a part of.

158
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,480
 And it beats for you here tonight.

159
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:28,480
 You need only come to him.

160
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,480
 That's what one group of people is saying.

161
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:40,480
 They're saying that traditional masculinity is a mistake, that we don't need men to act like men because, well, that can become toxic.

162
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,480
 Here's the thing.

163
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:51,480
 It's just as toxic to neuter a man of God when he has a God-given design and he has been asked to become something that he is not.

164
00:10:51,480 --> 00:11:00,480
 That's why young men today, they're experiencing higher levels of anxiety and purposelessness and loneliness than at any other point in human history.

165
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:02,480
 You see, I need you to lean in on this.

166
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,480
 We do not need to suppress masculinity.

167
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:07,480
 We need to sanctify it.

168
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:09,480
 And that's what Christ wants to do.

169
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:14,480
 He wants to sanctify your manhood, men.

170
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:21,480
 And then for women, the popular concept of our culture is that you don't need no man because who run the world?

171
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,480
 Exactly.

172
00:11:22,480 --> 00:11:26,480
 Just this week, I was reading a feminist article.

173
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:30,480
 Now, admittedly, it was a radical feminist article.

174
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:44,480
 And yet as I was reading it, the idea that the author was presenting was this concept that the male population has become redundant, that women can do everything that men can do.

175
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:46,480
 They can fulfill every role that men can.

176
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:49,480
 And in addition to that, they can have children.

177
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,480
 Now, I want to be very clear.

178
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:55,480
 I am in no way speaking to the capabilities of women in this moment.

179
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:58,480
 I believe that women are wildly capable for so much.

180
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:01,480
 My wife is a boss.

181
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:03,480
 Like she is a leader in business.

182
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:05,480
 She is a manager of people.

183
00:12:05,480 --> 00:12:13,480
 And she has literally built companies, ideas, campaigns, strategies that have literally moved the needle at a cultural level.

184
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:16,480
 She is altogether amazing.

185
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:21,480
 And she is one example of what is true of so many women in this room.

186
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:28,480
 And yet what I know to be true of my wife, what she would say is that she nonetheless needs me.

187
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,480
 Why does she need me?

188
00:12:29,480 --> 00:12:36,480
 Because no single person, single gender can rightly image God without the other.

189
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,480
 Men need women.

190
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:45,480
 And then she would also say that she knows she cannot fulfill the mandate given her by God to fill the earth and subdue it.

191
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:52,480
 Because despite what that author is saying, and no matter how much inventory you have in the sperm bank,

192
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:55,480
 at some point, God is going to need to show back up and make their contribution.

193
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:56,480
 You know?

194
00:12:56,480 --> 00:13:02,480
 Men and women are required to do all that God has desired.

195
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:07,480
 And so if you're here and you're thinking along the same lines of this camp,

196
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:17,480
 I just want you to know that you're given so much access to womanhood in and of your own God-given right.

197
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:21,480
 And yet it is through the presence of men that even more realms of womanhood are made available.

198
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:27,480
 As you consider becoming a wife, you consider being a mother, you consider being a grandmother.

199
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:28,480
 Men need women.

200
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,480
 Women need men.

201
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,480
 I could go on.

202
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:32,480
 I could give you more examples.

203
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:35,480
 But we need to get into the text.

204
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,480
 My point is very simple.

205
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:41,480
 In a world where the conversation around manhood and womanhood feels a lot like he said/she said,

206
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:45,480
 we need to consider what has God said?

207
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:49,480
 What has he said is the purpose of being a man?

208
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:51,480
 What is the purpose of being a woman?

209
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:56,480
 We need to consider what are the problems in becoming a man and what are the problems in becoming a woman?

210
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:01,480
 We need to actually consider what is the path to becoming a true man of God?

211
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:04,480
 What is the path to becoming a true woman of God?

212
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:06,480
 And that's what we're going to do over the course of this series.

213
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:10,480
 Over six weeks' time, we are going to answer these three questions.

214
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:17,480
 And if that math ain't mathing for you, the way we're going to do it is every week we're going to focus on one gender.

215
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:19,480
 And so it's guys tonight.

216
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:21,480
 Ladies, you're invited.

217
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,480
 And it's girls next week.

218
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,480
 And then it's guys the week after that.

219
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:27,480
 And it's girls the week after that.

220
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:36,480
 All the way until we have answered what is the purpose, what are the problems, and what is the path towards manhood and womanhood?

221
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,480
 And this is intentional.

222
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:43,480
 Like it isn't just because I want to give the boys a look behind the female curtain.

223
00:14:43,480 --> 00:14:49,480
 Like it's not that I'm trying to give us space to really evaluate things that we should not know.

224
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:56,480
 Instead, there is stuff here that will deeply serve the other if in fact we are informed.

225
00:14:56,480 --> 00:15:02,480
 You see, we live in a culture that has convinced us that for one gender to win, the other gender must lose.

